    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d368">

                <pb facs="0374" n="362" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg362"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24591/9–2644: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-28T16:00:00-04:00">September 28,
                            1944—4 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>590. The Iranian Minister, under instructions from his Government, has informed
                    the Department that rumors are current in Tehran that American troops may be
                    withdrawn from the country in the near future. The Minister expressed the hope
                    of his Government that certain American military supplies, including notably
                    food, drugs and clothing, might be left in Iran when the American troops
                    withdraw. He said that you have already been approached by the Iranian Foreign
                    Minister in this matter.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d368-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>The Minister was informed that according to information the Department has
                    received from the War Department, no action in regard to the movement of
                    American troops in Iran is being contemplated, other than the possible
                    withdrawal of some troops as a result of the discontinuance of the truck
                    route.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d368-f1" n="32" xml:id="d368-f1-content">
                <p>Mohammed Saed, Iranian Prime Minister and also Minister for Foreign Affairs,
                    addressed a note dated September 25 in the above sense to the Ambassador in
                    Iran, which the latter transmitted to the Department in his despatch No. 56,
                    September 29, <hi rendition="#italic">infra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
